[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110461985","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108913#issuecomment-3110461985","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108913","id":3110461985,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65ZeIh","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T21:59:06Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T22:00:30Z","body":"You probably need to enable **Vertex Color > Is sRGB** in StandardMaterial3D.\n\nOn a custom shader, you can replicate this behavior by adding the following code:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e0603aeda3ce0e15c5843f5202172a56f3ff5534/scene/resources/material.cpp#L1220-L1225\n\nIt's strange that you would have to do this though, given glTF vertex colors are normally in linear space, not sRGB: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82994#issuecomment-1752114917","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110461985/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110597041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108913#issuecomment-3110597041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108913","id":3110597041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65Z_Gx","user":{"login":"FuWan722","id":182037074,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmqUg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182037074?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722","html_url":"https://github.com/FuWan722","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T22:15:30Z","updated_at":"2025-07-23T22:18:02Z","body":"Sadly that just make it worse\n\nHere is without modifying the COLOR\n\n<img width=\"700\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/243a84e7-5323-4ef9-99c7-ed4c99287f57\" />\n\n\nWith sRGB conversion\n<img width=\"700\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7c6e8a9-a84a-4ad2-a72d-924bb775e205\" />\n\n\nWhat I somewhat expect\n<img width=\"700\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce569153-dabb-4560-bf08-2f36880511bd\" />\n\nIt seems Godot COLOR is not linear, or something wrong with Blender export vertex color, because each stripes supposed to represent RGB\n=[0.2, 1.0, 0.0] \n=[0.4, 1.0, 0.0] \n=[0.6, 1.0, 0.0] \n=[0.8, 1.0, 0.0] \n=[1.0, 1.0, 0.0]\nat each vertex, but its not in this case. Thats why I think my code `COLOR=pow(COLOR,vec4(0.42));` works because it \"straighten\" back the [0,...1] range.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110597041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110785786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108913#issuecomment-3110785786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108913","id":3110785786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65atL6","user":{"login":"FuWan722","id":182037074,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmqUg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182037074?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722","html_url":"https://github.com/FuWan722","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FuWan722/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-23T22:42:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-24T00:03:27Z","body":"I just rechecked in Blender, and it actually interpolated my vertex color (even though I click set vertex color value instead of using the brush). This seems like an issue with Blender color picker not being in linear space and not Godot.\n\nTo those wanting to fix this issue, I cant seem to find any way to change this in Blender so you either power your COLOR generated by blender by 0.42 in your gdshader or power the color you actually want by 2.2 (=1/0.42) in Blender vertex paint.\n\n2.2 is the power conversion from sRGB to RGB\n\n<img width=\"1269\" height=\"550\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a0546ed9-7a4c-4f09-9540-4c2d976916b9\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3110785786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]